    "result_text": "Build succeeds and the full suite (the single acceptance test `coreJoinersShareHouseholdId`) is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe \"allow same-address owner when `sharesHousehold=true`\" half was already scaffolded (`sharesHousehold` DTO field + `existsOwnerInHousehold`). I implemented the missing half \u2014 the persisted, stable, shared `householdId` \u2014 placing each piece where it belongs:\n\n**New `HouseholdIdGenerator`** (`service/`, mirrors the existing `CustomerCodeGenerator`) \u2014 owns the \"household\" concept: canonicalizes last name + address (trim / collapse whitespace / lower-case) and derives a deterministic, stable id (`HH-` + 12 hex of SHA-256 of the canonical key). Because it's deterministic, the same household always maps to the same id regardless of registration order.\n\n**`Owner` entity** \u2014 added a `household_id` column with getter/setter.\n\n**`ClinicServiceImpl`** \u2014 extracted a shared `findHouseholdMembers(...)` helper (now reused by both `existsOwnerInHousehold` and the new logic, and it single-sources address canonicalization through the generator). Added `assignHousehold(owner)`, which reuses an existing member's id or generates one, assigns it to the new owner, and **backfills** any existing members lacking it \u2014 so \"both\" members end up with the same id. Added to the `ClinicService` interface.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 restructured the household branch: if a household already exists, reject with 409 unless `sharesHousehold` is true, otherwise call `assignHousehold` before saving.\n\n**`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 `householdId` auto-maps onto the response DTO; explicitly ignored on the inbound `OwnerFieldsDto \u2192 Owner` mapping (consistent with the existing `id`/`pets` ignores).\n\n**Schema/contract** \u2014 added `householdId` (readOnly) to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml` so the generated DTO exposes it, and added the `household_id` column to all four DB schemas (hsqldb \u2014 used by the tests \u2014 plus h2/mysql/postgres for consistency).\n\nThe test creates owner `a`, then `b` and `c` at the same name+address with `sharesHousehold=true`; both are allowed and their `householdId` values match and are non-blank. \u2714",
